       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the maximum metformin dose. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis looks like a possible typo. Did you mean one of these?\n\n- **850 mg** PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **425 mg** PO three times daily (this isn't a standard tablet strength, so 500 mg is more typical)\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 4250 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy or your attending first."
